\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Model geometry. The brittle elastic plate (thickness $H$, Young's modulus $E$, Poisson's ratio $\nu $) overlies either a Newtonian viscous half-space (viscosity $\eta $) or, in its visco-elastic extension (Section~\ref {sec:maxwell_model}), a Maxwell half-space of the same viscosity $\eta $ that additionally shares the plate's elastic moduli $E,\nu $ -- the Elastic-Viscous (EV) and Elastic-Visco-Elastic (EVE) cases, respectively. Dike intrusions open the rift by $b$ at intervals $T$; the horizontal surface displacement $u(x,t)$ is positive in the $+x$ direction. The parameter $a = EH/[2\eta (1-\nu ^2)]$ sets the characteristic velocity that couples elastic and viscous deformation.}}{3}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:schematic}{{2}{3}{Model geometry. The brittle elastic plate (thickness $H$, Young's modulus $E$, Poisson's ratio $\nu $) overlies either a Newtonian viscous half-space (viscosity $\eta $) or, in its visco-elastic extension (Section~\ref {sec:maxwell_model}), a Maxwell half-space of the same viscosity $\eta $ that additionally shares the plate's elastic moduli $E,\nu $ -- the Elastic-Viscous (EV) and Elastic-Visco-Elastic (EVE) cases, respectively. Dike intrusions open the rift by $b$ at intervals $T$; the horizontal surface displacement $u(x,t)$ is positive in the $+x$ direction. The parameter $a = EH/[2\eta (1-\nu ^2)]$ sets the characteristic velocity that couples elastic and viscous deformation}{figure.2}{}}
