\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces EV STEP response to a single dike intrusion of opening $b$ at $t=0$, at six times $\tau /\tau _R \in \{0.001,\,0.25,\,0.5,\,1,\,2,\,3\}$, one per row. The Maxwell time $\tau _R=\eta /\mu _m$ (Section~\ref {sec:maxwell_model}) serves here only as a time unit, the same one used for the EVE counterpart (Figure~\ref {fig:maxwell_halfspace_step}). Left column: surface velocity $v^{\text  {STEP}}$ (Equation~\ref {eq:stepv}; solid, left axis, in units of $b/\tau _R$) and displacement $u^{\text  {STEP}}$ (Equation~\ref {eq:step}; dashed, right axis, in units of $b$), counted from the instant after the intrusion, so that the two flanks move apart symmetrically and each tends to $\pm b/2$ at the axis. The dashed vertical line marks $x=a\tau $, the position of the velocity peak. Middle column: speed $|v|$ in the half-space beneath the plate (filled contours, logarithmic scale, in units of $b/\tau _R$), computed from the surface velocity with Equation~(\ref {eq:halfspace_kernel}) over $|x|\le 30H$ and $z\le 30H$. Arrows show the flow direction only and have a fixed length. Right column: the same field enlarged to $|x|\le H$, $z\le H$ beneath the rift axis, with the same colour scale. Speeds outside the colour bar range $[0.01,\,1]$ are clipped to its end colours. All lengths are scaled by the plate thickness $H$. Parameters: $H=10$~km, $E=40$~GPa, $\nu =0.25$, $\eta =5.2\times 10^{18}$~Pa\,s, giving $a\approx 1.3$~km\,yr$^{-1}$ and $a\tau _R/H=1/(1-\nu )\approx 1.33$.}}{5}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:viscous_halfspace_step}{{3}{5}{EV STEP response to a single dike intrusion of opening $b$ at $t=0$, at six times $\tau /\tau _R \in \{0.001,\,0.25,\,0.5,\,1,\,2,\,3\}$, one per row. The Maxwell time $\tau _R=\eta /\mu _m$ (Section~\ref {sec:maxwell_model}) serves here only as a time unit, the same one used for the EVE counterpart (Figure~\ref {fig:maxwell_halfspace_step}). Left column: surface velocity $v^{\text {STEP}}$ (Equation~\ref {eq:stepv}; solid, left axis, in units of $b/\tau _R$) and displacement $u^{\text {STEP}}$ (Equation~\ref {eq:step}; dashed, right axis, in units of $b$), counted from the instant after the intrusion, so that the two flanks move apart symmetrically and each tends to $\pm b/2$ at the axis. The dashed vertical line marks $x=a\tau $, the position of the velocity peak. Middle column: speed $|v|$ in the half-space beneath the plate (filled contours, logarithmic scale, in units of $b/\tau _R$), computed from the surface velocity with Equation~(\ref {eq:halfspace_kernel}) over $|x|\le 30H$ and $z\le 30H$. Arrows show the flow direction only and have a fixed length. Right column: the same field enlarged to $|x|\le H$, $z\le H$ beneath the rift axis, with the same colour scale. Speeds outside the colour bar range $[0.01,\,1]$ are clipped to its end colours. All lengths are scaled by the plate thickness $H$. Parameters: $H=10$~km, $E=40$~GPa, $\nu =0.25$, $\eta =5.2\times 10^{18}$~Pa\,s, giving $a\approx 1.3$~km\,yr$^{-1}$ and $a\tau _R/H=1/(1-\nu )\approx 1.33$}{figure.3}{}}
