\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Self-similarity collapse of the step response in the EV model and in the Fickian \citet  {foulger1992post} model, each plotted against its own self-similarity variable ($\xi = x/(at)$ for EV, $\xi _F = x/\sqrt  {\kappa t}$ for Foulger) for $\xi >0$. Both models start from the same opening $b$, so both displacements equal $b/2$ at the rift axis; the curves are not normalised. (a)~Displacement $u/b$: EV (\ref {eq:step_dimless}) and Foulger $\tfrac  {1}{2}\mathrm  {erfc}(\xi _F/2)$. (b)~Velocity $t\,v/b$: EV (\ref {eq:stepv_dimless}) and Foulger (\ref {eq:foulger_v_dimless}). In both panels the dotted guide marks the $\xi ^{-1}$ power-law slope the EV curve approaches; the Fickian curves instead decay as a Gaussian. Because $\xi $ and $\xi _F$ use different length scales, only the shapes of the two tails, not their horizontal offset, are comparable.}}{6}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:step_selfsimilar}{{4}{6}{Self-similarity collapse of the step response in the EV model and in the Fickian \citet {foulger1992post} model, each plotted against its own self-similarity variable ($\xi = x/(at)$ for EV, $\xi _F = x/\sqrt {\kappa t}$ for Foulger) for $\xi >0$. Both models start from the same opening $b$, so both displacements equal $b/2$ at the rift axis; the curves are not normalised. (a)~Displacement $u/b$: EV (\ref {eq:step_dimless}) and Foulger $\tfrac {1}{2}\mathrm {erfc}(\xi _F/2)$. (b)~Velocity $t\,v/b$: EV (\ref {eq:stepv_dimless}) and Foulger (\ref {eq:foulger_v_dimless}). In both panels the dotted guide marks the $\xi ^{-1}$ power-law slope the EV curve approaches; the Fickian curves instead decay as a Gaussian. Because $\xi $ and $\xi _F$ use different length scales, only the shapes of the two tails, not their horizontal offset, are comparable}{figure.4}{}}
