\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces EV RSS for $T=5\tau _R$, in the same layout as the STEP response (Figure~\ref {fig:viscous_halfspace_step}), at six phases $\tau /T \in \{0.001,\,0.2,\,0.4,\,0.6,\,0.8,\,0.99\}$, one per row. Left column: surface velocity $v_{\text  {RSS}}$ (Equation~\ref {eq:vcss}; solid, left axis, in units of $V=b/T$) and displacement accumulated since the most recent intrusion $u_{\text  {RSS}}$ (Equation~\ref {eq:ucss}; dashed, right axis, in units of $b$). The dashed vertical line marks $x=a\tau $, the velocity-peak position of the most recent intrusion alone. Middle column: speed $|v|$ in the half-space (filled contours, logarithmic scale, in units of $V$), computed with Equation~(\ref {eq:halfspace_kernel}) over $|x|\le 4.5\,aT$ and $z\le 4.5\,aT$. Arrows show the flow direction only and have a fixed length. Right column: the same field enlarged to $|x|\le 0.15\,aT$, $z\le 0.15\,aT$ beneath the rift axis, with the same colour scale. Speeds outside the colour bar range $[0.01,\,1]$ are clipped to its end colours. Parameters as in Figure~\ref {fig:viscous_halfspace_step}, giving $aT \approx 67$~km.}}{8}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
