\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Convergence of the finite-sum velocity (\ref {eq:finite_sum_v}) to the RSS (\ref {eq:vcss}) at phase $\tau /T=0.5$, for $N = 1$, 3, 10 and 2000 past intrusions (solid curves) and the RSS (dashed). Velocity is normalised by $b/T$ and distance by $aT$. The deficit of the truncated sum grows with distance, approximately as $(b/\pi T)\arctan [x/(NaT)]$: with $N=10$, the sum matches the RSS near the axis but remains below the far-field plateau $b/(2T)$ (dotted) for $x \gtrsim aT$.}}{9}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
