\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces EVE STEP response to a single dike intrusion of opening $b$, with the same layout, units, colour scale and parameters as the EV STEP response (Figure~\ref {fig:viscous_halfspace_step}) and $\tau _R=\eta /\mu _m$ from the shared-modulus closure (Equation~\ref {eq:tau_R_shared}). Rows show $\tau /\tau _R \in \{0^+,\,0.25,\,0.5,\,1,\,2,\,3\}$. The first row is the limit $\tau \to 0^+$, evaluated in closed form: unlike the EV case, the surface velocity there is finite, reaching $b/(2\tau _R)$ at the axis (Equation~\ref {eq:maxwell_plateau}). Left column: surface velocity $v^{\text  {EVE}}$ (Equation~\ref {eq:maxwell_vel}; solid, left axis, in units of $b/\tau _R$) and displacement $u^{\text  {EVE}}$ (Equation~\ref {eq:maxwell_step}; dashed, right axis, in units of $b$), counted from the instant after the intrusion. The dashed vertical line marks $x=a\tau $, the EV velocity-peak position, for direct comparison with Figure~\ref {fig:viscous_halfspace_step}. Middle column: speed $|v|$ in the half-space (filled contours, logarithmic scale, in units of $b/\tau _R$), computed with Equation~(\ref {eq:halfspace_kernel}) over $|x|\le 30H$ and $z\le 30H$. Arrows show the flow direction only and have a fixed length. Right column: the same field enlarged to $|x|\le H$, $z\le H$ beneath the rift axis, with the same colour scale. Speeds outside the colour bar range $[0.01,\,1]$ are clipped to its end colours.}}{10}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
