\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces EVE RSS for $T=5\tau _R$, in the same layout, units and colour scale as the EV RSS (Figure~\ref {fig:viscous_halfspace_css}), with $\tau _R=\eta /\mu _m$ from the shared-modulus closure (Equation~\ref {eq:tau_R_shared}), at six phases $\tau /T \in \{0^+,\,0.2,\,0.4,\,0.6,\,0.8,\,0.99\}$, one per row. The first row is the limit $\tau \to 0^+$, computed from its exact form: the displacement since the most recent intrusion is zero, and the surface velocity at the axis, $(b/2\tau _R)/(1-e^{-T/\tau _R})\approx 2.5\,V$ (Equation~\ref {eq:maxwell_rss_jump}), lies beyond the plotted range and is clipped at $2\,V$. Left column: surface velocity $v_{\text  {RSS}}^{\text  {EVE}}$ (Equation~\ref {eq:maxwell_css_v}; solid, left axis, in units of $V=b/T$) and displacement accumulated since the most recent intrusion $u_{\text  {RSS}}^{\text  {EVE}}$ (Equation~\ref {eq:maxwell_css_u}; dashed, right axis, in units of $b$). The dashed vertical line marks $x=a\tau $, the EV velocity-peak position of the most recent intrusion alone, for direct comparison with Figure~\ref {fig:viscous_halfspace_css}. Middle column: speed $|v|$ in the half-space (filled contours, logarithmic scale, in units of $V$), computed with Equation~(\ref {eq:halfspace_kernel}) over $|x|\le 4.5\,aT$ and $z\le 4.5\,aT$. Arrows show the flow direction only and have a fixed length. Right column: the same field enlarged to $|x|\le 0.15\,aT$, $z\le 0.15\,aT$ beneath the rift axis, with the same colour scale. Speeds outside the colour bar range $[0.01,\,1]$ are clipped to its end colours. Parameters as in Figure~\ref {fig:viscous_halfspace_step}, giving $aT \approx 67$~km.}}{12}{figure.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:maxwell_halfspace_css}{{9}{12}{EVE RSS for $T=5\tau _R$, in the same layout, units and colour scale as the EV RSS (Figure~\ref {fig:viscous_halfspace_css}), with $\tau _R=\eta /\mu _m$ from the shared-modulus closure (Equation~\ref {eq:tau_R_shared}), at six phases $\tau /T \in \{0^+,\,0.2,\,0.4,\,0.6,\,0.8,\,0.99\}$, one per row. The first row is the limit $\tau \to 0^+$, computed from its exact form: the displacement since the most recent intrusion is zero, and the surface velocity at the axis, $(b/2\tau _R)/(1-e^{-T/\tau _R})\approx 2.5\,V$ (Equation~\ref {eq:maxwell_rss_jump}), lies beyond the plotted range and is clipped at $2\,V$. Left column: surface velocity $v_{\text {RSS}}^{\text {EVE}}$ (Equation~\ref {eq:maxwell_css_v}; solid, left axis, in units of $V=b/T$) and displacement accumulated since the most recent intrusion $u_{\text {RSS}}^{\text {EVE}}$ (Equation~\ref {eq:maxwell_css_u}; dashed, right axis, in units of $b$). The dashed vertical line marks $x=a\tau $, the EV velocity-peak position of the most recent intrusion alone, for direct comparison with Figure~\ref {fig:viscous_halfspace_css}. Middle column: speed $|v|$ in the half-space (filled contours, logarithmic scale, in units of $V$), computed with Equation~(\ref {eq:halfspace_kernel}) over $|x|\le 4.5\,aT$ and $z\le 4.5\,aT$. Arrows show the flow direction only and have a fixed length. Right column: the same field enlarged to $|x|\le 0.15\,aT$, $z\le 0.15\,aT$ beneath the rift axis, with the same colour scale. Speeds outside the colour bar range $[0.01,\,1]$ are clipped to its end colours. Parameters as in Figure~\ref {fig:viscous_halfspace_step}, giving $aT \approx 67$~km}{figure.9}{}}
